<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48403" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θέρειος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ος</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			Ael.
		</span></i> (v. infr.): (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θέρος</span>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of summer, in summer</i>,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐχμὸς θ</span>.
			<i>summer</i>-drought, <i><span class="en">
				Emp.
				111.7
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δρέπανον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Orph.
					<u>H.</u>
					40.11
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καρποί</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				18
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θέρειος ὥρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ael.
					<u>NA</u>
					2.25
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θερεία</span>, 
				Ion.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-είη</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥρα</span>), ἡ,= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θέρος</span>, <i>summer-time, summer</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.189
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mir.</u>
				841a25
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				5.1.3
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				<u>PTeb.</u>
				27.60
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii B.C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				19.58
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θερίᾳ</span>)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">;
				θερείης</span>
			<i>in summer</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				81
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεσούσης θ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				1.63
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὸ τὴν θερείαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					3.24
				</span></i>
			: pl., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θερείαις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>I.</u>
					2.41
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			
				Sup.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θερείτατος, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">η</span>,
					<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span></span>, <i>very hot</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Arat.
				149
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Th.</u>
				460
			</span></i>.—In Prose <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θερινός</span>
			is the more common form.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
